Superseded: see sglang_spec_decode.patch + sglang_spec_decode_install.py
========================================================================

This file used to carry the sglang call sites for aiter.ops.triton.draft_sample
as a hand-applied diff. They now live in ``sglang_spec_decode.patch`` and are
installed idempotently by ``sglang_spec_decode_install.maybe_install()``, which
``aiter/__init__.py`` calls at import time.

Ops in ``aiter.ops.triton.draft_sample`` used by those call sites:

  draft_sample(logits, temperatures)            -> (q, q(X), X)
  verify_target_probs(logits, temperatures, n)  -> softmax(logits / repeat(T, n))
  shard_argmax_partials / shard_argmax_reduce   -> vocab-parallel greedy pick
  greedy_argmax(logits)                         -> single-rank lowest-id argmax

Each site logs one line on first use ("aiter fused <tag> active, first shape
...") so a deployment can confirm the branch was actually taken.

One correction to the claim this file used to make. "Both sites are
import-guarded, so reverting aiter silently restores the torch chain" is *not*
true of the vocab-parallel greedy pick: the draft's logits processor has its
all-gather disabled before cuda-graph capture, so losing the aiter half leaves
the gather off and the pick reducing this rank's slice alone -- a shard-local
id, on every rank, with no error. ``_init_vocab_parallel_greedy`` therefore asks
``spec_utils.vocab_parallel_argmax_available()`` first and keeps the gather when
the answer is no.
